        model: 'I’d say it in private, with respect for what he knows: “You’re probably right about the rack. But if you give the answer, Kees learns to wait for yours. Try asking questions 3 and 4 and then hold back: which obstacle are you working on, what’s your next step? If he picks something else, let him try it; you’ll both learn.” And I’d offer to watch a few cycles and give him feedback afterwards.',
